WEBVTT
 
00:00.000 --> 00:07.400
Joanna Jimbuku is a nurse. 

00:07.450 --> 00:11.980
She lives and works in North Australia. 

00:11.980 --> 00:17.940 
Her boss is Bob Mills, a flying doctor. 

00:17.980 --> 00:25.060
He and Joanna go everywhere in the Bluebird, Bob's plane. 

00:25.100 --> 00:30.630 
One morning in August, Joanna answers the phone.

00:30.720 --> 00:37.420
"Hello?" she says. "Dr. Mills' office." 

00:37.500 --> 00:47.870
Then, a baby. "Yes, I see. And you're in Womara? Okay." 

00:47.940 --> 00:52.050
"We can be there in half an hour." 

00:52.150  -> 00:58.300
Five minutes later, Joanna and Bob are in the Bluebird.

00:58.480 --> 01:03.800
"How old is this baby?" asks Bob. 

01:03.900 --> 01:08.000
"Eighteen months," says Joanna.

01:08.100 --> 01:12.400
After a moment, Bob looks at her. 

01:12.500 --> 01:17.400
"Womara's near your hometown, isn't it?"

01:17.500 --> 01:23.500
"Yes. That's right." Joanna smiles. 

01:23.600 --> 01:26.900
"It's a very small place." 

01:26.950 --> 01:29.840
She looks out of the window.

01:30.000 --> 01:33.700
"There it is," she says. 

01:33.800 --> 01:39.120
"Can you see between those trees and the river?"

01:39.840 --> 01:46.900
Down on the ground, eight or nine people are waiting for the flying doctor. 

01:47.000 --> 01:52.050
They take him and Joanna to a small house. 

01:52.100 --> 01:59.400
The baby's mother, Jane, is inside it. 

01:59.500 --> 02:03.600
Bob looks at the little girl for 20 minutes.

02:04.000 --> 02:12.900
Then, he says, "I'm sorry, but Mary is very, very ill." 

02:13.000 --> 02:19.280
"It's her heart. She must go to a hospital in Sydney."

02:20.240 --> 02:27.130
"Sydney?" says Jane. "Yes." 

02:27.200 --> 02:31.500
Bob puts his hand on the woman's arm. 

02:31.500 --> 02:36.320
"But it's okay. You can go with her."

02:36.800 --> 02:45.500
Jane looks sad. "How? I've got six other children." 

02:45.600 --> 02:51.600
"I can't just leave them." Suddenly, Joanna has an idea.

02:51.800 --> 02:55.900
"Wait a minute," she says. 

02:56.000 --> 03:00.200
"Why don't I go to Sydney with Mary?" 

03:00.250 --> 03:05.200
"After all, I'm on holiday for two weeks after today."

03:06.160 --> 03:10.200
"Good idea," says the flying doctor. 

03:10.300 --> 03:16.900
They look at Jane. "Okay," she says. 

03:17.100 --> 03:23.440
24 hours later, Joanna arrives in Sydney for the first time.

03:25.280 --> 03:27.900
Two nurses are waiting at the airport. 

03:28.00 --> 03:34.080
They drive her and Mary very fast to a big hospital.

03:38.500 --> 03:42.200
Then they take Mary into room 308. 

03:42.300 --> 03:45.440
A doctor's waiting there.

03:48.000 --> 03:55.840
"Hello," he says. "My name's Paul Griffin." Joanna smiles at him.

03:56.320 --> 04:04.300
"Hello." Then she asks the nurses, "Can I help?" 

04:04.400 --> 04:07.840
Joanna spends all day at the hospital.

04:09.280 --> 04:12.600
But after eight hours, she's very tired. 

04:12.700 --> 04:15.520
Paul Griffin sees this.

04:17.920 --> 04:23.400
"Why don't you stay with me and my wife tonight?" he asks. 

04:23.500 --> 04:27.200
"Thanks," says Joanna. 

04:27.300 --> 04:30.240
"That's really nice of you."

04:33.680 --> 04:37.920
At six o'clock, she and Paul drive to his house.

04:39.920 --> 04:44.000
There, Joanna meets Paul's wife, Fran. 

04:44.100 --> 04:50.000
She meets their daughter too. Her name is Polly.

04:50.800 --> 04:56.000
After dinner, Paul shows Joanna to her room. 

04:56.100 --> 04:58.800
Joanna sits on the bed.

05:00.800 --> 05:05.280
"Is Mary going to be okay?" she asks.

05:07.280 --> 05:10.800
"I don't know," Paul replies. 

05:10.900 --> 05:17.760
Then he says, "but we're going to do everything we can."

05:20.720 --> 05:25.480
After that, Joanna goes to the hospital every day. 

05:25.550 --> 05:31.440
She helps the nurses and sits beside Mary's bed.

05:33.920 --> 05:37.300
For three days, nothing happens.

05:37.400 --> 05:43.440
Then one afternoon, Joanna's reading a book in room 308.

05:44.240 --> 05:52.360
Suddenly, she hears a noise. "What's that?" she thinks. 

05:52.400 --> 05:55.520
Then she hears it again.

05:59.920 --> 06:05.540
She stands up and walks to Mary's bed. 

06:05.600 --> 06:11.680
"Mary, it's you. You're sitting up. You're talking."

06:12.640 --> 06:16.720
She runs out of the room and finds Paul.

06:18.320 --> 06:24.640
"Quick, Dr. Griffin," she says. "It's Mary. Come and see."

06:27.040 --> 06:31.760
Later that day, Joanna telephones Bob Mills.

06:33.200 --> 06:38.640
"Yes, that's right. Mary's going to be okay,"

06:39.520 --> 06:45.520
she says with a big smile. "I can bring her home next week."

06:47.280 --> 06:52.700
That evening, the Griffins take Joanna to an expensive restaurant. 

06:52.800 --> 06:56.470
Joanna sits next to the window. 

06:56.520 --> 07:02.300
Outside, she can see the lights of Sydney. 

07:02.400 --> 07:07.040
"This is beautiful," she says.

07:09.600 --> 07:11.300
Next morning at breakfast, 

07:11.400 --> 07:17.500
Paul says, "Joanna, you can stay here at home today. 

07:17.600 --> 07:26.400
After all, Mary's okay now." "No thanks," says Joanna. 

07:26.500 --> 07:29.700
"I want to be with her." 

07:29.800 --> 07:35.500
At the hospital, Paul sees Sister Clark. 

07:35.600 --> 07:44.880
"One of my girls is leaving next week and we need someone new," she says.

07:46.960 --> 07:53.300
"What about Joanna Jimbuku? She's a very good nurse. 

07:53.400 --> 07:56.720
Do you think she wants a job here?"

07:57.600 --> 08:02.650
"Me?" says Joanna that evening. 

08:02.700 --> 08:09.000
She looks at Paul. "Why not?" he says. 

08:09.100 --> 08:16.500
"After all, Sister Clark's right. You're a very good nurse." 

08:16.600 --> 08:25.200
Joanna is quiet. "Don't say anything now," Paul tells her.

08:26.000 --> 08:30.600
"Just think about it. That's all I'm asking." 

08:30.700 --> 08:39.600
He walks away, then turns. "But not for too long, okay?"

08:41.200 --> 08:43.300
The next day is Saturday. 

08:43.400 --> 08:47.760
Joanna goes to the hospital and sees Mary.

08:48.480 --> 08:53.200
"Hello, little one," she says. 

08:53.300 --> 09:03.120
"You're going home on Monday." Then she thinks, "Or are we going home?"

09:05.760 --> 09:10.560
Two hours later, Fran and Polly meet Joanna for lunch.

09:11.440 --> 09:19.920
"Oh, Joanna. You are going to stay in Sydney, aren't you?" says Polly.
 
09:20.400 --> 09:24.800
"I don't know," says Joanna.

09:28.320 --> 09:33.400
Later in the afternoon, Joanna goes for a long walk. 

09:33.520 --> 09:40.130
The weather is hot. She watches the people in the streets. 

09:40.260 --> 09:47.680
She looks at all the shops, cinemas, museums and theaters too.

09:50.320 --> 09:53.300
"Sydney's great," she thinks. 

09:53.400 --> 09:59.280
"It's very beautiful and there's a lot to see and do."

10:00.240 --> 10:06.880
"But do I really want to live here? That's the question."

10:10.480 --> 10:14.800
Across the street, there's a shop window. 

10:14.900 --> 10:18.800
Joanna turns and looks in it.

10:19.920 --> 10:24.140
She can see a big painting of some red hills. 

10:24.220 --> 10:28.540
"Wait a minute," she thinks. 

10:28.600 --> 10:35.280
"I know that place. It's near Womara."

10:38.000 --> 10:41.760
Ten minutes later, a man comes out of the shop.

10:44.320 --> 10:47.620
"Are you okay?" he asks. 

10:47.720 --> 10:53.120
Joanna smiles. Her eyes are wet.

10:53.440 --> 11:02.880
"Yes," she says. "I'm fine. Really? I'm fine."

11:05.000 --> 11:09.400
Two days later, Bob gets into the Bluebird. 

11:09.500 --> 11:17.120
Joanna is with him. She waves goodbye to Jane and Mary.

11:17.600 --> 11:23.440
Bob starts the plane and pushes his hat back.

11:25.440 --> 11:31.200
"Listen, thanks for everything, Joanna. He says.

11:31.300 --> 11:33.900
This is in Sydney, I mean. 

11:34.000 --> 11:36.960
It's a beautiful city, isn't it?"

11:39.280 --> 11:43.160
Joanna looks at the red hills of Womara. 

11:43.200 --> 11:46.160
Then she smiles too.

11:47.120 --> 11:53.920
"Yes," she says. "But it's good to be home."
